    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Climate-resilient and inclusive international fintech institute facility developed 
Indicator: By 2026, IFI building designed and constructed, adopting green building standards and climate adaptation measures, with gender-sensitive and accessibility features for persons with disability and diverse SOGIESC. 
Progress/Status: The contract for the construction of the IFI Building was signed on April 22, 2024, officially marking the beginning of the project. Construction work officially commenced on May 1, 2024, which set the stage for the project&amp;apos;s overall timeline.
Excavation work, up to the foundation level, was successfully completed by July 2024. This milestone paved the way for the initiation of the foundation works in September 2024, a crucial step in the construction process.
The foundation works are progressing smoothly, with a particular focus on the raft foundation. Due to the substantial size of the foundation, it has been divided into three parts for efficient execution. Part 1 of the raft foundation has been fully completed, while Parts 2 and 3 are currently under construction.
Further work is also underway on Pour 1, which includes essential structural elements such as the retaining wall, columns, and shear walls. These components are crucial for stabilizing the building and ensuring the continued advancement of the project. 
Data Source: Detailed design and drawings of the IFI and associated facilities and construction supervision reports 
