     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Institutional capacity to manage operating systems and business models developed 
Indicator: By 2028, business and financial model for sustainable operation of the IFI finalized, including the strategy note for setting up an endowment fund 
Progress/Status: The business and financial model for the sustainable operation of the IFI, along with the strategy note for establishing an endowment fund, will be finalized by the selected partners in the upcoming quarter. The IFI will primarily generate revenue through fees from short, medium, and long-duration programs, with additional income from consulting services. Cash flows will be managed through program revenues, gap funding, and working capital infusions from institutions. Projections from the selected consortium indicate that IFI (CS03) will achieve financial viability and self-sustainability by the end of its fourth year. This financial stability will reduce external reliance while generating a consistent surplus, which can be reinvested in resources to stay at the forefront of technological advancements, maintain relevance, and attract top talent. This ongoing cycle of attracting high-quality faculty and increasing student engagement will ensure the IFI&amp;apos;s long-term sustainability. 
